<title>USA: Brazil coffee areas cold but no damaging cold see.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee areas cold but no damaging cold see.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's coffee areas will be cold early on Tuesday but no but no damaging cold is forecast, private forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Low temperatures will once again dip into the upper 30s and 40s on Tuesday morning before moderating by mid to late this week. There is no damaging cold anticipated.</p>
<p>Cold temperatures were also recorded in the Brazilian coffee belt Monday morning with lows dropping into the upper 30s and 40s.</p>
<p>East-central Brazil will be dry on Tuesday with highs of 59 to 73 degrees. Lows on 40 to 51 are forecast for Wednesday morning and 45 to 55 on Thursday before milder weather Friday and Saturday, WSC said.</p>
</text>
